# Day 6 – Challenges

## Challenge 1 – Understanding Trigger Timing

Initially, understanding the difference between before and after triggers was challenging.

I learned that validation should normally happen before the record is saved, while actions that depend on a successful save belong after the record is saved.

## Challenge 2 – Separating Trigger and Business Logic

Another challenge was understanding why the Trigger should not contain all the business logic.

I learned to keep the Trigger short and delegate business processing to ApplicationService or a Handler.

## Challenge 3 – Avoiding Duplicate Logic

Some validation logic existed in both the Handler and Service.

I cleaned the architecture so that CGPA and closing-date validation are handled by ApplicationService.

## Challenge 4 – Testing Trigger Behaviour

Testing required creating Application records with different Student and Job combinations.

I tested invalid CGPA conditions and verified that Salesforce rejected the Application with a meaningful error message.

## What I Improved

- Apex Trigger design
- Before/after trigger understanding
- Service-layer architecture
- Bulkified Apex
- Error handling using addError()
- Salesforce deployment and testing
